    }
   ],
   "id": "p052"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p053.s01",
     "source": "."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p053"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p054.s01",
     "source": "”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p054"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p055.s01",
     "source": "The lady walked into the cave, and was kindly asked by the wee bodies to take a chair and sit down, while they still continued their spinning."
    },
    {
     "id": "p055.s02",
     "source": "She observed that ilk ane’s mouth was thrawn away to ae side, but she didna venture to speer the reason."
    },
    {
     "id": "p055.s03",
     "source": "They asked why she looked so unhappy, and she telt them that it was she was expected by her husband to be a good spinner, when the plain truth was that she could not spin at all, and found herself quite unable for it, having been so delicately brought up; neither was there any need for it, as her husband was a rich man."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p055"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p056.s01",
     "source": "“Oh, is that a’?” said the little wifies, speaking out of their cheeks alike."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p056"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p057.s01",
     "source": "“Yes, and is it not a very good a’ too?” said the lady, her heart like to burst wi’ distress."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p057"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p058.s01",
     "source": "“We could easily quit ye o’ that trouble,” said the wee women."
    },
    {
     "id": "p058.s02",
     "source": "“Just ask us a’ to dinner for the day when your husband is to come back."
    },
    {
     "id": "p058.s03",
     "source": "We’ll then let you see how we’ll manage him.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p058"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p059.s01",
     "source": "So the lady asked them all to dine with herself and her husband, on the day when he was to come back."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p059"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p060.s01",
     "source": "When the gudeman came hame, he found the house so occupied with preparations for dinner, that he had nae time to ask his wife about her thread; and, before ever he had ance spoken to her on the subject, the company was announced at the hall door."
    },
    {
     "id": "p060.s02",
     "source": "The six ladies all came in a coach-and-six, and were as fine as princesses, but still wore their gowns of green."
    },
    {
     "id": "p060.s03",
     "source": "The gentleman was very polite, and showed them up the stair with a pair of wax candles in his hand."
    },
    {
     "id": "p060.s04",
     "source": "And so they all sat down to dinner, and conversation went on very pleasantly, till at length the husband, becoming familiar with them, said—"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p060"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p061.s01",
     "source": "“Ladies, if it be not an uncivil question, I should like to know how it happens that all your mouths are turned away to one side?”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p061"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p062.s01",
     "source": "“Oh,” said ilk ane at ance, “it’s with our constant spin-spin-spinning .”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p062"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p063.s01",
     "source": "“Is that the case?” cried the gentleman; “then, John, Tam, and Dick, fie, go haste and burn every rock, and reel, and spinning-wheel in the house, for I’ll not have my wife to spoil her bonnie face with spin-spin-spinning .”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p063"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p064.s01",
     "source": "And so the lady lived happily with her gudeman all the rest of her days."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p064"
  }
 ]
}